Package: dash
Type: Package
Title: Depth-Aware Structural-Zero and Hellinger Test for Microbiome Differential Abundance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    c(
        person("Yiqian", "Zhang", email = "zhang.16383@osu.edu",
               role = c("aut", "cre")),
        person("Zihan", "Zhu", email = "zihan.zhu@yale.edu",
               role = "aut")
    )
Description: A two-part differential abundance test for microbiome count data.
    DASH combines a structural-prevalence score test with a present-conditional
    abundance test. The structural-prevalence component uses a per-taxon
    structural-zero mixture model with a left-censored normal observation
    component, estimated by an expectation-maximization algorithm. The
    abundance component uses Hellinger-Riemann intrinsic coordinates (HRIC),
    auxiliary posterior-presence weights, a censoring-correction nuisance
    covariate, and a robust affine correction for the compositional background.
    Uncertainty in the affine-corrected abundance coefficient is estimated using
    a joint sample-level HC3 sandwich variance, with asymptotic-normal inference.
    The two component p-values are combined per taxon by a Bonferroni min-P rule
    and a Cauchy combination rule.
